# GMS says this OVERRIDES Vessel of Light rather than stacking with it, which
# nothing here can express: every source of damage sums. So what it grants is
# the DIFFERENCE -- Vessel of Light maxed is 10% damage and 40 attack, and the
# two together come to the 25% and 60 GMS's override reaches. A Paladin who
# never finished the 2nd job skill gets less than GMS would give them, which is
# the price of the reading and is small.
#
# Its HP recovery is dropped, as the user asked; the status resistance and the
# damage taken are already the whole of what Vessel of Light grants, so this
# adds nothing to either. Both figures below are per Light Charge times the
# five charges a Paladin holds, exactly as Vessel of Light folds them.
#
# The strikes and the reach are the rest of the skill and the reason SkillBoost
# exists: a strike each to Divine Charge and Blast, and two more enemies for
# Divine Charge by the sixth level -- GMS's ceil(L/5).
name: "Greater Vessel of Light"
skill_order: 8
description:
  "The light within you grows greater still. Increases Damage and Attack "
  "Power, and strengthens Divine Charge and Blast."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_PALADIN
max_level: 10
exceeds_master_level: true
base {
  damage_pct: 0.105
  attack: 11
}
per_level {
  damage_pct: 0.005
  attack: 1
}
boost {
  skill_name: "Divine Charge"
  lines: 1
  max_enemies: 1
  max_enemies_per_level: 0.2
}
boost {
  skill_name: "Blast"
  lines: 1
}
